From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] Build the aic8800 USB driver against Linux 6.18

Applies to radxa-pkg/aic8800 tag 5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-8. On the previous
pin, 4.0+git20250410.b99ca8b6-5, the vendor source failed on 6.18.36 with 13
errors across five kernel API changes: MODULE_IMPORT_NS now takes a string
literal, the wakeup_source create/add/remove/destroy quartet is gone in favour
of register/unregister, del_timer[_sync] became timer_delete[_sync], from_timer
became timer_container_of, and several cfg80211 ops and helpers gained link_id
or radio_idx parameters.

The 5.0 tag guards every one of those call sites itself, with
LINUX_VERSION_CODE branches for 6.12 / 6.13 / 6.15 / 6.16 / 6.17 in
aicwf_tcp_ack.c, rwnx_main.c, rwnx_radar.c, rwnx_rx.c, rwnx_wakelock.c,
aic_priv_cmd.c and aic_bluetooth_main.c, so those hunks are gone. What is left:

- rwnx_cfg80211_get_tx_power() is new in 5.0 (the previous pin had the op
  commented out) and is wired into rwnx_cfg80211_ops with the pre-6.14
  prototype. 6.18.36 expects (wiphy, wdev, int radio_idx, unsigned int link_id,
  int *dbm), include/net/cfg80211.h:4991. Both parameters are accepted and
  ignored. Radxa's packaging fixes the same site with
  debian/patches/fix-linux-6.14-build.patch and fix-linux-6.17-build.patch,
  which our build does not apply.
- Four call sites our build never compiles but that still name removed timer
  APIs: three in aicwf_sdio.c (CONFIG_SDIO_SUPPORT = n,
  aic8800_fdrv/Makefile:60) and one del_timer_sync() inside #if 0 in
  rwnx_cfg80211_del_iface(). Carried unchanged from the previous revision of
  this patch, so the subtree names no removed timer API.

Replacements read out of the 6.18.36 tree: timer_delete / timer_delete_sync at
include/linux/timer.h:167,166, timer_container_of at :132, get_tx_power at
include/net/cfg80211.h:4991. The in_irq() that fix-linux-6.19-build.patch
replaces still exists in 6.18.36 (include/linux/preempt.h:141) and is left
alone.

Not fixed here, noted because the previous revision of this patch edited the
line: on kernels >= 6.12, rwnx_radar_cancel_cac() in 5.0 reports
NL80211_RADAR_CAC_FINISHED on a cancelled CAC (rwnx_radar.c:1621), where its
own < 6.12 branch and the previous pin report NL80211_RADAR_CAC_ABORTED.

